      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To study the association between two single nucleotide polymorphisms (rs4810485 and rs1535045 in CD40 gene) and Kawasaki disease (KD) in Han Chinese children."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "A case-control study was performed on 184 children with KD and 206 normal controls. The polymorphisms of two SNPs in CD40 gene were detected using PCR-RFLP."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "There were no significant differences in the genotype distribution and allele frequency of SNP rs4810485 in CD40 gene between the KD and normal groups (P&gt;0.05). The genotype distribution of SNP rs1535045 in CD40 gene in the KD group was significantly different from the control group (P&lt;0.05). T allele of SNP rs1535045 was shown as a risk factor for development of KD (OR=1.592, 95%CI: 1.182-2.144, P=0.004). There were no association between the polymorphisms of the two SNPs and coronary artery lesions (P&gt;0.05)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "SNP rs1535045 may be associated with the development of KD in Han Chinese children, while SNP rs4810485 may not."
        }
      ]},
